{
  "name": "SameKindNameUnderTwoTypes",
  "comment": "Two types can each have a kind of the same name — each found through its own parent\n(ruling 2, decision 774). A kind's name is unique only under its parent (names on two\nlevels, like files in folders), so number's `short` and duration's `short` are\ndifferent kinds, each reached only through its own type. Red today for the kind.name\nhalves (held under the same stopgap as DecimalIsANumber): today `%x!type.kind.name%`\nreads null because kind isn't a navigable type at run — stage 1 (the probe on number)\nfixes number's half, stage 3 extends it to every family (duration included).",
  "step": [
